  "question": {
    "text": "A nucleus of mass 20 u emits a <math><mi>γ</mi></math> -photon of <math><mn>6</mn><mi>&nbsp;<mn>&nbsp;M</mn><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></mi></math> . If the emission assume to occur when nucleus is free and rest, then the nucleus will have kinetic energy nearest to <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>Take</mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>u</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mn>k</mn><mn>g</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> ."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>10</mn><mn>&nbsp;k</mn><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>&nbsp;k</mn><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0.1</mn><mi> </mi><mn>&nbsp;k</mn><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mni></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>100</mn><mi> </mi><mn>&nbsp;k</mn><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
